{"id": "q0043", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1444618742, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "John decides to take up an odd hobby of speed talking.  His normally speaking speed is 150 WPM.  After training his speed is 2.5 times faster than his starting speed.  How long would it take him to speak 10 pages if each page has 450 words per page?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0043.wav", "input_sha256": "7511979c576dfe6b7baf56db69b2a66a2b5852357ac54a1a34eb69f2c68bb239", "input_samples": 320200, "input_s": 20.012, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.2841, "act": 0.9985, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so John's starting speed is 15 0 words per minute. After training, he speaks 2. 5 times faster, so that would be 1 50 times 2. 5. Let' s calculate that: 1 50 times 2 is 3 00, and 15 0 times 0.5 is 75, so adding those together gives 3 75 words per minute.Now, each page has 4 50 words, and there are 10 pages, so the total number of words is 4 50 times 10, which equal s 4, 50 0 words.To find out how long it takes to speak all those words at his new speed, we divide the total words by his speaking rate: 4, 5 00 divided by 3 75. Let' s do that division: 4, 500 divided by 37 5 equals 1 2 minutes. So, it would take him 12 minutes to speak 10 pages at his increased speed.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, 