{"id": "q0062", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 321549282, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Dexter has five pigs. Each one eats 4 pounds of feed, twice a day. If Dexter ordered 300 pounds of feed, how many pounds of feed is left after a week?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0062.wav", "input_sha256": "5a3a06aa57496346a4242089421ae2f546556db35ea4f183e556151d4c41bf8f", "input_samples": 211400, "input_s": 13.213, "n_real_chunks": 14, "score": 0.0563, "act": 0.9992, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Each pig eats 4 pounds twice a day, so that' s 8 pounds per pig per day. For five pigs, that's 5 times 8, which is 40 pounds per day. Over seven days, they eat 40 times 7, which equal s 2 80 pounds. D exter ordered 300 pounds, so subtracting the amount eaten, 3 00 minus 2 80 leaves 2 0 pounds of feed left after a week.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 13, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 23, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0062_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "6499dd07b487f0b99e6f6c74d8b8db24cd885cb994f017ff170b704aa971f8b3", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 23.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.068, 1.126, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.072, 2.13, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.07, 3.129, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.071, 4.131, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.071, 5.13, 1,