{"id": "q0097", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3839400866, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "Mark's car breaks down and he needs to get a new radiator.  The cost for a new radiator is $400 but he goes to get it at a junk shop and gets it for 80% off.  He then hires a mechanic to install it and it takes 3 hours at $50 an hour.  How much did he pay?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0097.wav", "input_sha256": "45f43b7c397a695e39ba151b7ea0f7ae6a02665a18d449d0a28dcc09674722ed", "input_samples": 332200, "input_s": 20.762, "n_real_chunks": 21, "score": 0.1553, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Okay, so he got the radiator for 80% off of $400. So that's going to be $ 3 20 because 20% of $4 00 is $80. And then it takes three hours at $50 an hour to install it. So that's going to be $15 0. So in total, he paid $3 20 plus $1 5 0, which is $ 4 7 0. So Mark paid $470 in total.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 20, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 31, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0097_conservative_local.wav", "sha256": "6999e6e3cc3a2809facdc9b770558ce0536861dbb1ee04ccedbaef6af728ac27", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 31.04}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.069, 1.125, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.071, 2.129, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.07, 3.128, 1, 0