{"id": "q0242", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "conservative", "tier": "conservative", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 580437262, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "1bd884090589f25ac8e99f9bb754f4b90b4c7a09d6887616d0aefbdba25a74d4", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.9057239890098572, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 1, "query": "The lowest point on Earth is the bottom of the Mariana Trench at a depth of 35,840 feet below sea level. The highest point on Earth is the summit of Mt. Everest at a height of 29,028 feet above sea level. Which of the following is the best estimate of the distance between the lowest and highest points on Earth?\n\nA. 75,000 feet\nB. 65,000 feet\nC. 55,000 feet\nD. 60,000 feet\nE. 7,000 feet\nF. 64,000 feet\nG. 70,000 feet\nH. 50,000 feet\nI. 6,000 feet\nJ. 80,000 feet\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0242.wav", "input_sha256": "4e7d28604264753fb9e1a4de2796558a79cb54b5e50911b3dfb049871f86ce90", "input_samples": 677800, "input_s": 42.362, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.161, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So the lowest point is 3 5,8 45 feet below sea level and the highest point is 2 9,2 8 feet above sea level. To find the total distance between them you add the depth of the ten ch to the height of Everest because they are on opposite sides of sea level. That means you add 35, 84 5 plus 29,2 8 which equal s about 6 5,0 73 feet. Looking at the options the closest estimate is B 6 5,000 feet.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 38, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 27, "feed_lag_max_ms": 444, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 